+Description:
+The reference C implementation of Argon2 (RFC 9106) by its authors, Daniel Dinu, Dmitry
+Khovratovich, Jean-Philippe Aumasson and Samuel Neves. Thoron uses Argon2id to derive the key that
+locks a portable copy's profile key from the person's passphrase (components/thoron_portable_key).
+The authors offer it under CC0 1.0 or Apache 2.0, at the user's option; Thoron takes it under
+Apache 2.0. LICENSE holds both texts, unchanged.
+
+Local Modifications:
+Only these files of the release tarball (phc-winner-argon2-20190702.tar.gz, SHA-256
+daf972a89577f8772602bf2eb38b6a3dd3d922bf5724d45e7f9589b5e830442c) are copied, unchanged, into src/
+with the release's own layout: include/argon2.h; src/argon2.c, core.c, core.h, ref.c, encoding.c,
+encoding.h, thread.c, thread.h; src/blake2/blake2b.c, blake2.h, blake2-impl.h, blamka-round-ref.h.
+The SIMD code (opt.c), the command-line tool, the test programs and the known-answer files are left
+out. BUILD.gn defines ARGON2_NO_THREADS, so the library starts no threads of its own. The unit tests
+of components/thoron_portable_key check the RFC 9106 Argon2id test vector (section 5.3), which is
+also the release's kats/argon2id.
